    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "530216",
        "date_added": "2026-11-20 13:12:47",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static analysis, not executed. Static x86-64 ELF, not packed. Plain-text TCP C2 at 169.128.70[.]53:7002 (IP also in Joe Sandbox 2010211; port from the code). Registers with `BOT|x86 cores=\u003cn\u003e ram=\u003cn\u003eKB`, then reads `!\u003cmethod\u003e \u003ctarget\u003e [port] [seconds]` lines (19 DDoS commands, e.g. !udp-gbps, !ovh-flood, !home-holder, !kill-all). Double fork, renames itself `[kworker/0:1]`. No persistence, scanner or exploit code, and no Mirai-style XOR config table, so I do not see support for the Mirai label. Write-up, YARA rule, IOCs: https://github.com/cyberpascal1101/linux-malware-research/tree/main/plaintext-ddos-bot"
      }
    ],
